{"parentUuid":"405459f5-6a5b-49bd-b850-ea6d38b78355","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a11eb425ca2c37694","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01B5eA8ARG6AD8EgHFu9ypmm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0124pjoduez9R7shzzwVvw8E","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"LIPIcs.CP.2025.42 Huub Dekker"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21123,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":252,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":21123},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":252,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21123,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":21123,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosGPfSy6AN8iMhaRceV","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"19c43696-2ce8-48e4-bfa3-6c8f3d57c7ae","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:49:39.220Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b3edd7ea-ef20-4f7f-9c1e-b69b35bbfb3c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a11eb425ca2c37694","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LCoMnWrH3hi1w1Qjxp8jfX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Huub solver \"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG\" CP 2025 Dekker Ignatiev Stuckey\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG Jip J. Dekker #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG (Short Paper)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG\",\"url\":\"https://alexeyignatiev.github.io/assets/pdf/disz-cp25-preprint.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP 2025 Accepted Papers\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/accepted_papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Alexey S. Ignatiev Optimisation group, FIT@Monash\",\"url\":\"https://alexeyignatiev.github.io/assets/pdf/cv.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/html/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's the information about the paper:\n\n## \"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG\" - CP 2025\n\nThe paper \"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG\" was authored by Jip J. Dekker, Alexey Ignatiev, Peter J. Stuckey, and Allen Z. Zhong, and was presented at the 31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025).\n\n**Key Contribution:**\n\nThe authors present Huub, an LCG (Lazy Clause Generation) solver built based on the IPASIR-UP interface to SAT engines. This modular design allows them to easily swap in any SAT solver that supports the interface, enabling the solver to benefit from the latest advancements in SAT solving technology.\n\n**Technical Details:**\n\nThe core engine of Huub is implemented in Rust 1.81.0 using CaDiCal 2.1.3 as the back-end SAT solver, although in theory any SAT solver supporting the IPASIR-UP interface could be used. Huub is an open-source LCG solver, and it is used to evaluate the performance of using modern SAT features and explore several design and engineering decisions for LCG solvers.\n\nThe paper includes comparisons with state-of-the-art solvers like Chuffed and CP-SAT, using benchmarks from the MiniZinc Challenge 2024.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0e49709d-258d-4f9e-95d6-ad90848941f6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:49:43.034Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b3edd7ea-ef20-4f7f-9c1e-b69b35bbfb3c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"19c43696-2ce8-48e4-bfa3-6c8f3d57c7ae","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a11eb425ca2c37694","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0124pjoduez9R7shzzwVvw8E","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"LIPIcs.CP.2025.42 Huub Dekker\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG Jip J. Dekker #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG (Short Paper)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of ...\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/LIPIcs.CP.2025.0/LIPIcs.CP.2025.0.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - huub-solver/huub: CP+SAT solver framework built to be reliable, performant, and extensible · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/huub-solver/huub\"},{\"title\":\"Unit Types for MiniZinc - DROPS - Schloss Dagstuhl\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.10\"},{\"title\":\"Cargo Routing Optimization in Liner Shipping Networks\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.11\"},{\"title\":\"Unit Types for MiniZinc - Monash University\",\"url\":\"https://research.monash.edu/en/publications/unit-types-for-minizinc/\"},{\"title\":\"CP/SAT Doctoral Program 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcpdp25.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Anytime and Exact Search for Planning Problems: How to explore a DP-based state transition graph with A*, CP and LS? (Invited Talk)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.2\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about LIPIcs.CP.2025.42:\n\nThe paper LIPIcs.CP.2025.42 is titled \"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG\" and was presented at the 31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025). \n\nThe paper presents Huub, an LCG (Lazy Clause Generation) solver built based on the IPASIR-UP interface to SAT engines. This modular design allows the solver to easily swap in any SAT solver that supports the interface, enabling the solver to benefit from the latest advancements in SAT solving technology.\n\nNote: The search results show that the first author is Jip J. Dekker (not Huub Dekker). The paper is authored by Jip J. Dekker, Alexey Ignatiev, Peter J. Stuckey, and Allen Z. Zhong. The solver itself is named \"Huub,\" which appears to be why you may have seen that name in connection with this paper.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9ef1bafc-3748-43db-af4e-9b2b50bbf74e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:49:45.446Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"19c43696-2ce8-48e4-bfa3-6c8f3d57c7ae","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"405459f5-6a5b-49bd-b850-ea6d38b78355","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a11eb425ca2c37694","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MjLdrG7zv56BTSJtDSsjvL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Huub solver IPASIR-UP LCG lazy clause generation github\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"huub-solver/huub: A Lazy Clause Generation ...\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/huub-solver/huub\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG (Short Paper)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42\"},{\"title\":\"Huub: Lazy Clause Generation Solver Software - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/artifact/10.4230/artifacts.24103\"},{\"title\":\"Huub: Lazy Clause Generation Solver\",\"url\":\"https://zenodo.org/records/15591853\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Modern and Modular SAT for LCG Jip J. Dekker #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol340-cp2025/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42/LIPIcs.CP.2025.42.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"AllenZzw (Allen) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/AllenZzw\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR 2 Workgroup · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ipasir2\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL SAT Conference, July 7, 2023\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/talks/sat2023_talk.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"Chuffed, a lazy clause generation solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Huub, IPASIR-UP, and lazy clause generation:\n\n## Huub Solver\n\nHuub is an efficient library for developing constraint-based decision or optimization systems with learning capabilities that combines the strengths of constraint programming with the learning and proof machinery of Boolean satisfiability solving. Huub is a Lazy Clause Generation (LCG) solver with a focus on modularity and maintainability in addition to speed.\n\n## GitHub Repository\n\nThe Huub source code is available at https://github.com/huub-solver/huub\n\n## IPASIR-UP and Lazy Clause Generation\n\nLazy Clause Generation is an architecture for building Constraint Programming solvers using an underlying Boolean Satisfiability engine, where the CP propagation engine lazily creates clauses that define the integer variables and impose problem restrictions, and the SAT engine uses the clausal model to reason and search.\n\nUsing a new interface to SAT engines, IPASIR-UP, an LCG solver can be constructed which can swap out the underlying SAT engine with any that supports the interface. While IPASIR-UP can be used to construct an LCG solver, it requires a change of perspective from the solver designer—most LCG solvers use a SAT solver as a component, but when using the IPASIR-UP interface, it is the SAT solver that runs the solving process and makes calls to the external propagation engine.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b83a1f52-d8a5-49c7-ad69-2bbd59071baa","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:49:46.792Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"405459f5-6a5b-49bd-b850-ea6d38b78355","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
