{"parentUuid":"d1d09935-15cf-4b00-9872-b32deb082ad6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a11eb425ca2c37694","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01NnZneX7U6j56GrKRzB7QTe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UKnBTA3ZGpWJL5nAJR1VnH","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://huub.solutions","prompt":"Extract all documentation: install, getting started, API examples in Rust, supported constraints list, propagator trait, examples for routing/no_overlap/cumulative, FlatZinc and MiniZinc usage. Are there Python bindings?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2011,"cache_read_input_tokens":66262,"output_tokens":503,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2011},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":503,"cache_read_input_tokens":66262,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2011,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosNwQaXpcUs2ptHEYfu","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1d573090-28ae-4620-8218-a5dba2e96da7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:10.501Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c7dadf5d-d5df-4577-bd23-0d8a0f359823","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a11eb425ca2c37694","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018v65PmrRkKPjLvBUozY7ay","type":"tool_result","content":"# Huub README Summary\n\nBased on the provided web page content, here's what's documented:\n\n## Project Overview\nHuub is described as \"an efficient library for developing constraint-based decision or optimization systems and applications with learning capabilities.\" It integrates constraint programming with Boolean satisfiability solving.\n\n## Key Characteristics\nThe library emphasizes three main qualities:\n- **Reliability**: Well-tested with state-of-the-art preprocessing, implemented in Rust\n- **Performance**: Combines strong propagation with modern solving techniques\n- **Extensibility**: Allows custom propagators, branchers, and SAT solver replacement\n\n## Available Resources\nThe README provides links to:\n- Official website (huub.solutions)\n- Package registry on crates.io\n- API documentation on docs.rs\n\n## Citation Information\nFor academic or professional use, the creators provide a BibTeX citation with DOI 10.5281/zenodo.15591852, authored by Dekker, Stuckey, and Zhong under the MPL-2.0 license.\n\n## Notable Gaps\nThe provided README excerpt does not include:\n- Installation or build instructions\n- MiniZinc integration details\n- Rust API usage examples\n- Python binding information\n- Supported constraint types documentation\n\nThese details likely appear in the full documentation on the linked external resources."}]},"uuid":"c6152c40-8f0a-41e2-9d21-45ad7e81b54f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:11.166Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c7dadf5d-d5df-4577-bd23-0d8a0f359823","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d1d09935-15cf-4b00-9872-b32deb082ad6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a11eb425ca2c37694","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNttE8ecafaH7ikwQoH4Ph","type":"tool_result","content":"# Huub Workspace Overview\n\n## Workspace Members\n\n1. **crates/huub** - Core solver library\n2. **crates/huub-cli** - Command-line interface tool\n3. **xtask** - Build automation tasks\n\nDefault members are huub and huub-cli.\n\n## Project Metadata\n\n- **Version:** 0.1.0\n- **License:** MPL-2.0\n- **Edition:** 2024\n- **Repository:** github.com/huub-solver/huub\n- **Categories:** algorithms, mathematics, science\n- **Keywords:** sat, lcg, flatzinc, minizinc, optimization\n\n## Dependencies\n\n**Primary Dependencies:**\n- clap (4.6.1) - CLI argument parsing with derive macros\n- serde/serde_json - Serialization framework\n- flatzinc-serde (0.5.0) - FlatZinc format support\n- pindakaas (0.2.3) - SAT solver with external propagation\n- tracing/tracing-subscriber - Structured logging\n\n**Utilities:**\nanstream, bon, clap_complete, ctrlc, dyn-clone, humantime, itertools, mimalloc, rangelist, rustc-hash, tracing-test\n\n**Development Tools:**\nexpect-test, divan (benchmarking), codspeed-divan-compat\n\nThe project emphasizes code quality through comprehensive linting rules for Rust and Clippy, targeting unsafe code documentation, proper API visibility, and consistent coding patterns."}]},"uuid":"ab17bedf-d6e5-4b15-bad7-771c9090853c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:13.201Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d1d09935-15cf-4b00-9872-b32deb082ad6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1d573090-28ae-4620-8218-a5dba2e96da7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a11eb425ca2c37694","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UKnBTA3ZGpWJL5nAJR1VnH","type":"tool_result","content":"# Huub Documentation Summary\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, here's what's available:\n\n**Documentation Resources:**\nThe site offers \"API\" documentation via Rust docs and \"Docs\" section covering introduction and modelling topics. Navigation includes getting started guides and integration instructions.\n\n**Installation & Integration:**\nUsers can access Huub through MiniZinc with dedicated installation instructions, or work directly with the solver through programming interfaces for custom extensions.\n\n**Extensibility:**\nThe platform supports adding \"your own propagators, branchers, and even decision variable views,\" allowing customization for specific problem requirements.\n\n**Language Support:**\nThe webpage mentions Rust as the implementation language and MiniZinc compatibility. However, **the provided content does not address Python bindings, specific constraint lists, propagator trait details, routing/cumulative examples, or FlatZinc support.**\n\n**Limitations:**\nThis excerpt is a homepage overview. Comprehensive API examples, constraint specifications, and detailed propagator documentation would require accessing the full documentation portal referenced but not included in this content.\n\n**Community Support:**\nProfessional services through deciZns are available for integration assistance and performance optimization."}]},"uuid":"58d33fd2-3973-4680-a86d-4d0894c13690","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:16.281Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1d573090-28ae-4620-8218-a5dba2e96da7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
